        "original_id": "cd91b6fa-80da-540c-8d4c-ee4b28fb3817",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dmitri Usatov, Antonín Dvořák, Adolf Čech, Marie Červinková-Riegrová\n- Works: Eugene Onegin, The Devil and Kate\n- Roles: Lensky\n- Topics: opera productions, composer collaborators\n\nFacts:\n- In 1998, Dmitri Usatov sang the role of Lensky in an opera production of Eugene Onegin.\n- Antonín Dvořák composed the opera The Devil and Kate.\n- Adolf Čech, a friend of Antonín Dvořák, helped prompt Antonín Dvořák to create The Devil and Kate.\n- Marie Červinková-Riegrová, another friend of Antonín Dvořák, wrote the libretto for The Devil and Kate.\n- The Devil and Kate had more contributions from friends of its composer than the 1998 Eugene Onegin production in which Dmitri Usatov sang Lensky.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
