        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e9e43fe3-516e-555f-919d-aece95146601",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky, Konstantin Shilovsky, Antonín Dvořák, Adolf Wenig, Dmitri Usatov\n- Works: Eugene Onegin, The Devil and Kate, Mazeppa\n- Roles: M. Triquet, Lensky, Prince Gremin, Andrei\n\nFacts:\n- Eugene Onegin is an opera by Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky.\n- Konstantin Shilovsky, a friend of Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky, contributed M. Triquet's verses for Act 2, Scene 1 of Eugene Onegin.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky arranged the text for Lensky's arioso in Act 1, Scene 1 of Eugene Onegin and for almost all of Prince Gremin's aria in Act 3, Scene 1.\n- In 1881, Dmitri Usatov sang the role of Lensky in Eugene Onegin.\n- In 1884, Dmitri Usatov sang the role of Andrei in Mazeppa.\n- The Devil and Kate is an opera in three acts by Antonín Dvořák with a Czech libretto by Adolf Wenig.\n- The Devil and Kate is also known in Czech as Čert a Káča and has the identifiers Op. 112 and B.201.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "397a972e-0923-596a-8b33-13da68c54bbb",
        "text": "Page: Eugene Onegin (opera). Sentence: Eugene Onegin (Russian: Евгений Онегин , \"Yevgény Onégin\"), Op.\nPage: Eugene Onegin (opera). Sentence: Tchaikovsky's friend Konstantin Shilovsky contributed M. Triquet's verses in Act 2, Scene 1, while Tchaikovsky himself arranged the text for Lensky's arioso in Act 1, Scene 1, and almost all of Prince Gremin's aria in Act 3, Scene 1.\nPage: The Devil and Kate. Sentence: The Devil and Kate, Op.\nPage: The Devil and Kate. Sentence: 112, B.201, (\"Čert a Káča\" in Czech) is an opera in three acts by Antonín Dvořák to a Czech libretto by Adolf Wenig.\nPage: Dmitri Usatov. Sentence: There he sang the role of Lensky in \"Eugene Onegin\" in 1881 and the role of Andrei in \"Mazeppa\" in 1884.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
